WEBVTT

00:05:27.396 --> 00:05:30.116
But then once you find it,
you need to find your sisters.

00:05:30.116 --> 00:05:31.516
You need to find other people

00:05:31.556 --> 00:05:33.676
if we're actually
going to change structures.

00:05:33.676 --> 00:05:37.196
You cannot do that by yourself,
and that's where the power of we comes in.

00:05:37.196 --> 00:05:39.196
So me and we and that we're all powerful.

00:05:39.196 --> 00:05:41.516
That's the second thing
I wanted to mention here.

00:05:41.556 --> 00:05:42.756
And the third and final,

00:05:42.796 --> 00:05:44.916
although there's many
big topics in the book,

00:05:44.916 --> 00:05:47.916
is this idea that anything
that has come before

00:05:47.956 --> 00:05:50.756
can be undone and redone.

00:05:50.796 --> 00:05:54.196
I think sometimes we think of big things
like structures and systems,

00:05:54.196 --> 00:05:56.476
and we think that's just how it is

00:05:56.516 --> 00:05:58.796
and we have to operate
within those contexts.

00:05:58.836 --> 00:06:02.276
Well, I interviewed over 500 women
of color in writing this book,